<title>USA: Newport News Shipbuilding sets two-part debt deal.</title>
<headline>Newport News Shipbuilding sets two-part debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-tranche debt issue from Newport News Shipbuilding Inc was priced in the 144A private placement market on Thursday, according to lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities.</p>
<p>BORROWER NEWPORT NEWS SHIPBUILDING INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 8.625 PCT  MATURITY 12/01/2006</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 06/01/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BA2   YIELD  8.625 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BB	  SPREAD 250 BP     CALLABLE AFTER FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>BORROWER NEWPORT NEWS SHIPBUILDING INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 9.25 PCT   MATURITY 12/01/2006</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 06/01/1997 LAST MOODY'S B1    YIELD  9.25 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS    SPREAD 312.5 BP   CALLABLE AFTER FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1678</p>
